# Pending BDD specs (skeletons)

`.feature` files here are **acceptance-spec skeletons for unbuilt features**, each
tagged `@wip` and linked to its GitHub issue. They are deliberately **not bound** to
step definitions (no `scenarios(...)` call in `tests/step_defs/`), so pytest-bdd does
not collect them and CI stays green — an unbound scenario would otherwise raise
`StepDefinitionNotFound`.

Write scenarios in the project's `CONTEXT.md` ubiquitous language so they read the
same whether a human or an agent implements them later.

**When you implement one:** move its `.feature` up to `tests/features/`, add a
`tests/step_defs/test_<name>.py` with `scenarios("../features/<name>.feature")` plus
the step bindings, and drop the `@wip` tag.

